  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_buildr",
      "name": {
        "en": "Poncirus's Badge",
        "zh": "青枳证章",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_buildr",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Poncirus has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for preemptive penetration of the battlefield situation and active offense so as to secure leeway for deployment.\nThis operator shall hereby be appointed a Vanguard Operator during field operations to exercise Pioneer responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员青枳擅长抢先切入战局，通过进攻争取部署空间\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为先锋干员，行使尖兵职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_buildr",
      "name": {
        "en": "The Morning Star of the Homeseeker",
        "zh": "寻乡人的启明星",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_buildr",
      "description": {
        "en": "The setting sun drops and bathes the empty street in afterglow. In the wake of a light sea breeze, it prints faint golden light across the mottled sign. A shop awaiting customers, a damaged high-rise stretching up, a short young palm tree—these things, seemingly forever frozen in the past, warp with the rays in the warm ripple of twilight. She turns the corner, reaches to fiddle with a plank door on the silent roadside. Ash-blackened wood splinters and an ash-blackened lock fall away, throwing up dust just as ash-black as the rest of it. Through cracks in the ash peek the street's original lacquer of red and blue.\nThere's no longer a sharp protrusion to be found in this city blanketed by volcanic ash; it seems to stand forever at the other end of the young girl's dreamland. She can hardly connect the view before her eyes with the stories Grandpa used to tell her. This is where those long-gone fiery summers and crystal-clear blue sparkling waters were—somehow, it was only ever scenes like those where his younger self in the stories could stand firm with his back straight, chanting work songs and spilling sweat. Even as the stiff shoulder straps dig painfully into her body, she clutches onto her rucksack tight, hands smeared in grime.\nIt's wrong. This is wrong. No one could live in a fantasy of the past, no one could possibly keep their fervor lit forever with just memories for firewood, and no one should spend their life asleep just to go back to how it was. It'll all end, and then things are born anew. She's experienced frightful desperation, the challenges of self-rejection and Oripathy, the melancholy of finding you don't stand out within the crowd—she's been through all of it. She doesn't want to just keep chasing forever. She's going to welcome new goals, passions, and achievements. The sun has completely set by now; she sees the lights in the distance. Those are the rays of the new Siesta.\nSo long, childhood dreams. It's time to head for the next stop.",
        "zh": "垂落的斜阳将余晖抹过空荡的街头，伴着轻柔的海风一同擦出斑驳牌匾上的暗淡金光。等待光顾的商铺、往高处伸展的破损楼屋和尚未长成的低矮乔木，这些仿佛永远定格在过去的事物也都随着阳光晕开在荡漾的晚照之中。她拐过街角，伸手拨弄着路旁沉默的门板。灰黑的木条和灰黑的门锁垮落下来，溅起同样灰黑的尘埃，灰尘的缝隙中露出了街道原本蓝色和红色的油漆。\n被火山灰覆盖的城市已看不出曾经的犀利棱角，它仿佛伫立在女孩梦境的另一端。她难以把眼前的景象与爷爷曾经讲过的故事联系起来。那些早已逝去的火热夏天和晶莹透彻的海滨之蓝就是在这里——好像只有在那样的场景里，长辈口中的自己才能坚定地挺直腰杆，喊着号子挥洒汗水。即便牢固的肩带早已将她的身体勒得生疼，她还是用沾满灰尘的双手紧了紧背包的带子。\n不，不该这样。没有人会活在过去的幻境之中，没有人能够以回忆为柴薪长久地点燃激情，也没有人应该为了回到往昔而长睡不醒。一切都会结束，然后就是新生。她经历过可怕的绝望，那些自我否定和矿石病的困扰，那些在人群之中发现自己并不出彩的愁闷，她都挺过来了。她不愿只是继续追随，她会迎来新的目标、热情和成就。太阳已经完全落下，她看见了远方的灯火，那是新汐斯塔的光芒。\n再见，那些小时候的梦，是时候前往下一站了。",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
